MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_001: Hey there, lady-killer! Thanks for coming to chitchat!\nI've got a terribly interesting idea.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_002: Well... That was dangerous. So, NOT in a talky\nmood, are we?
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_003: If you wish a duel, ready your weapon.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_004: Tempting, but I was actually hoping we could\ntalk business instead.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_005: Seriously, do you assume every invitation to meet is\na battle proposition, or can you just not help yourself?
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_006: Fighting sustains me. It is my nature—that of\nmy house.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_007: You don't say... I'd heard tales of how strange House\nLamine could be...
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_008: But I guess you're living proof that they're true! \nHehe. Makes sense.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_009: What do you speak of?
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_010: Well, those who use Drake's treasures trade a tiny\npiece of their sanity for power in most cases...
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_011: Those like me, with Balor's blood, are born with a\ndecent resistance to it. But you and I aren't related.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_012: And yet, you have no trouble with Ink-Black\nWen whatsoever.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_013: Which meeeans...there's some secret to your house.\nEh, but I knew that much already.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_014: Hm.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_015: Fine, silently scowl if you want to... Before you tried\ncutting me in half, I'd asked you here for a reason.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_016: After we win this battle, I'm thinking of owning not\njust Dagda, but every continent there is.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_017: Part of that means connections. So I'd like to form\none with your noble Fódlan house.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_018: A business proposal? I am uninterested—\nseek another.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_019: Now, hold on. You're not a money man, I can see\nthat. But this is about improving our world, you see.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_020: If I can introduce one culture to another, imagine\nwhat new wonders they'd create together.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_021: Art, cuisine, all of it. The world would revolutionize\nitself into something more. Exciting, right?
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_022: My only wish is to kindle my soul with the spark of\nfiercest battle. We have no common ground.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_023: You sure about that, killer? Tell me, have you\npurchased anything lately?
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_024: A necklace, sold by a boy at market.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_025: Looks cheap. The inlay is alright, but the metal is\npoor, and the finish is sloppy, to put it kindly.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_026: Not to mention it looks like it was dragged over\nrocks. What possessed you to buy such a thing?
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_027: His eyes. They spoke to me.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_028: He told me it was a memento of his mother, his last.\nAnd he sold it only to earn bread for his sister.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_029: Yet his eyes shone with a resolve born from a spirit\nof utter ruthlessness.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_B_030: Huh. Interesting. Then maybe I'll give your shopping\nmethod a try...
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_001: What now? I rejected your proposal.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_002: I know, but I come with news! Remember the brat\nthat sold you that gods-awful necklace?
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_003: Turns out he's a notorious thief. But I figured hiring\nhim at Vandahl Trading would set him straight.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_004: So you acted on a whim. But will this stripling be of\nuse to you?
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_005: Well, even as a child, he managed to catch YOUR\neye, didn't he?
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_006: It's funny. I gave him a tour of one of our caravans,\nand he told me I'd overstaffed it.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_007: I tried explaining insurance—more eyes mean fewer\nmistakes. But he wasn't having it...
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_008: He even had the nerve to say, "Must be nice,\nknowing they have the space to fail."
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_009: "What, and you never screw up?" I asked him.\nAnd do you know what that little runt said?
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_010: That failure means death, I imagine.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_011: Yes. Pretty morbid, huh? Made it clear the boy has\nno sense of business...or banter.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_012: But there was such a fire in his eyes. One that tells\nme he's prepared to die for what he wants.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_013: And the people who heard him talking? They\nbecame lit with that same fire.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_014: I mean people who, no matter what I tell them,\nusually respond as if orders are some big hassle.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_015: Hrm...
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_016: His idea of "failure" affected those around him for the\nbetter. He connected with them, see?
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_017: So to forge a connection is to build a pathway\nto change?
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_018: Now you're getting it! So, you see why you should\nwork with me.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_019: You schemed simply to interest me? You are dogged.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_020: Eh, I've been called worse. It's true, we have our\ndifferences, and working together is an...experience?
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_021: But I like you. Because at our core, we're cut from\nthe same cloth, you and me.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_022: Good or bad, our goals come first. And it's everyone\nelse's job to keep up...if they even can.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_023: If our goals had even a tiny setback, we would have\nabandoned Dagda by now. But look...we're still here.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_024: Perhaps.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_025: Truth is, when people like us work together,\nwhatever happens, it's bound to be interesting.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_026: I see. When the war is over, I will hear you out.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_027: Then may the Zaratan be the vessel that carries you\nback to Fódlan, my friend.
MID_SE_Dit_Tal_A_028: Hehe. I'll even cover your boarding fee! Small price\nto pay when investing in the future.